      error <span class=k>instanceof</span> ZrizError <span class=p>&amp;&amp;</span>
      error<span class=p>.</span>code <span class=p>=== </span><span class=s>"aborted"</span>
    <span class=p>) {</span>
      <span class=k>return null</span><span class=p>;</span>
    <span class=p>}</span>
    <span class=k>throw</span> error<span class=p>;</span>
  <span class=p>}</span>
<span class=p>};</span>",
  ],
]
`;

exports[`content > writes accessibility as markdown 1`] = `
"# accessibility

> [llms.txt](https://zriz.dev/llms.txt)

zriz sets roles, keys and announcements. you write every word a screen reader says.

## label every control

zriz ships no words. give each control a name in your language:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Area aria-label="Crop area" />
<Cropper.Dial aria-label="Straighten" />
<Cropper.Zoom aria-label="Zoom" />
<Cropper.AspectGroup aria-label="Aspect ratio">
  <Cropper.AspectItem value={1}>square</Cropper.AspectItem>
</Cropper.AspectGroup>
<Cropper.Rotate aria-label="Rotate left">
  rotate
</Cropper.Rotate>
\`\`\`

in development, \`Area\`, \`Dial\` and \`Zoom\` warn once each in the console when nothing names them. an \`aria-label\`, an \`aria-labelledby\` or text inside all count. nothing checks the group or the buttons, so name those yourself.

## check what a screen reader hears

| part | what a screen reader gets |
| - | - |
| \`Area\` | one tab stop with \`role="group"\`, described by \`Instructions\` |
| \`Dial\` | a slider that reads "4 degrees" in your \`locale\`. \`format\` changes the wording |
| \`Zoom\` | a slider that reads "150%" in your \`locale\`. \`format\` changes the wording |
| \`AspectGroup\` | a \`radiogroup\` with one tab stop. each \`AspectItem\` is a radio. outside a group, an item is a button with \`aria-pressed\` |
| \`Rotate, Orientation\` | buttons. \`Orientation\` is disabled for a free, original or square crop |
| \`Flip\` | a toggle button. \`aria-pressed\` follows \`mirrored\` |
| \`Reset\` | a button that is \`hidden\` while nothing has changed |
| \`Image\` | an image named by its \`alt\`. without \`alt\`, nothing |
| \`Handle, Grid, Mask\` | hidden |

## describe the crop

\`Area\` points to \`Instructions\` with \`aria-describedby\`, so a screen reader reads its text when the crop gets focus:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Instructions>
  Arrows move the crop. Alt and arrows resize it.
</Cropper.Instructions>
\`\`\`

## announce changes

a moving crop has no text, so a screen reader stays silent without \`Announcer\`. after each commit it calls \`announce\` and speaks what it returns, or nothing for \`null\`. this one speaks the position and width after each keyboard change. dial keys commit as \`keyboard\` too, so it also speaks after an arrow press on the dial, on top of the dial's own value:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Announcer
  announce={({ center, size }, details) => {
    if (details.reason !== "keyboard") return null;
    const x = Math.round(center.x * 100);
    const y = Math.round(center.y * 100);
    const width = Math.round(size.width * 100);
    return \`Crop at \${x}%, \${y}%, \${width}% wide\`;
  }}
/>
\`\`\`

\`details.reason\` says what made the change, such as \`keyboard\`, \`dial\`, \`pan\` or \`orientation\`, and \`details.previous\` holds the crop before it. a message equal to the last one is spoken again.

## move everything with keys

every control works without a mouse. the keys live with each part: [crop area](https://zriz.dev/docs/crop-area.md), [dial](https://zriz.dev/docs/dial.md), [zoom](https://zriz.dev/docs/zoom.md) and [aspect ratio](https://zriz.dev/docs/aspect-ratio.md). buttons take enter and space like any button.

escape also cancels a photo drag or a handle drag.

a key pressed in a focusable child of \`Area\`, \`Dial\` or \`Zoom\` stays with that child, and ctrl, cmd and alt shortcuts stay with the browser. the one exception is alt + arrows on \`Area\`, which resizes the crop.

zriz adds no focus style and removes none, so the browser's default ring shows on \`Area\`, \`Dial\` and \`Zoom\`. [crop area](https://zriz.dev/docs/crop-area.md) shows a ring of your own.

## work without a drag

the dial, the handles and the photo pan need a drag, and keys do not replace that for someone who only has a pointer. wcag 2.5.7 asks for a way with single taps. \`Zoom\` already jumps on a press, for the rest add plain buttons that write to the cropper. pass a reason, so \`Announcer\` speaks these writes too:

\`\`\`tsx
"use client";

import { useCropper } from "@zriz/react";
import * as Cropper from "@zriz/react/cropper";

export const Editor = ({ src }: { src: string }) => {
  const cropper = useCropper();
  const turn = (by: number) => {
    cropper.setRotation(cropper.getValue().rotation + by, {
      reason: "keyboard",
    });
  };
  const move = (x: number, y: number) => {
    cropper.panBy(x, y, { reason: "keyboard" });
  };
  const resize = (by: number) => {
    const state = cropper.getCropState();
    if (state) {
      const crop = {
        ...state.crop,
        height: state.crop.height * by,
        width: state.crop.width * by,
      };
      cropper.setCropState(
        { ...state, crop },
        { keep: "centre", reason: "keyboard" }
      );
    }
  };
  return (
    <>
      <Cropper.Root cropper={cropper} src={src}>
        <Cropper.Viewport style={{ width: 480, height: 360 }}>
          <Cropper.Image />
          <Cropper.Mask />
          <Cropper.Area aria-label="Crop area" />
        </Cropper.Viewport>
      </Cropper.Root>
      <button onClick={() => turn(-1)}>straighten left</button>
      <button onClick={() => turn(1)}>straighten right</button>
      <button onClick={() => move(-0.01, 0)}>move left</button>
      <button onClick={() => move(0.01, 0)}>move right</button>
      <button onClick={() => move(0, -0.01)}>move up</button>
      <button onClick={() => move(0, 0.01)}>move down</button>
      <button onClick={() => resize(0.9)}>smaller crop</button>
      <button onClick={() => resize(1.1)}>larger crop</button>
    </>
  );
};
\`\`\`

## respect reduced motion

with \`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce\`, motion that zriz starts on its own gets shorter. drags, pinches and throws stay the same, so the photo follows your finger.

| motion | full | reduced |
| - | - | - |
| recentre | spring, about 460 ms | spring, about 250 ms |
| rotate 90° | about 300 ms | 150 ms |
| flip | spring, about 420 ms | 150 ms |
| aspect, reset | spring, about 460 ms | 150 ms |

\`motion="reduce"\` on \`Root\` forces the short motion, and \`motion="always"\` keeps the full one. \`Root\` shows \`data-reduced-motion\` while it is on.

the stylesheet's fades keep their length in both modes: the mask dims over 200 ms and comes back over 300 ms, and the grid fades in over 250 ms and out over 300 ms. after a gesture, the thirds grid and \`data-interacting\` on \`Root\` and \`Mask\` stay for 1380 ms. on \`Area\`, \`data-interacting\` clears when the gesture ends.

## api

### \`Announcer\`

renders a visually hidden \`<div role="status" aria-live="polite">\` anywhere inside \`Root\`.

- \`announce\` \`(value, details) => string | null\` required

  what to say after each commit. return \`null\` to stay quiet

### \`Instructions\`

renders a \`<div hidden>\` anywhere inside \`Root\`, which \`Area\` points to with \`aria-describedby\`. it has no props of its own. its children are the text.
"
`;

exports[`content > writes aspect-ratio as markdown 1`] = `
"# aspect ratio

> [llms.txt](https://zriz.dev/llms.txt)

buttons that lock the crop to a ratio such as 1:1 or 4:5, and one that swaps portrait and landscape.

the demo runs on the page at https\\://zriz.dev/docs/aspect-ratio.

## anatomy

the group and the orientation button go anywhere inside \`Root\`. each item names one ratio:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.AspectGroup aria-label="Aspect ratio">
  <Cropper.AspectItem value="free">free</Cropper.AspectItem>
  <Cropper.AspectItem value={1}>1:1</Cropper.AspectItem>
  <Cropper.AspectItem value={4 / 5}>4:5</Cropper.AspectItem>
  <Cropper.AspectItem value={16 / 9}>16:9</Cropper.AspectItem>
</Cropper.AspectGroup>
<Cropper.Orientation aria-label="Swap orientation">
  <svg
    aria-hidden="true"
    width={20}
    height={20}
    viewBox="0 0 20 20"
  >
    <path
      d="M3 6h14v8H3z"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      strokeWidth={1.5}
    />
  </svg>
</Cropper.Orientation>
\`\`\`

\`value\` is width divided by height, so \`4 / 5\` is 4:5. \`"free"\` drops the lock and \`"original"\` uses the photo's own ratio. picking an item springs the crop to it, with \`data-transition="morph"\` on \`Root\`.

on a round crop every item but \`value={1}\` is disabled. zriz ships these parts bare. the demo above uses the styles from the zriz site.

## lock one ratio with no buttons

pass \`aspect\` to \`Root\` and leave out the group. the crop keeps that ratio, and \`Reset\` returns to it:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Root src={photo} aspect={16 / 9}>
  <Cropper.Viewport style={{ height: 400 }}>
    <Cropper.Image />
    <Cropper.Mask />
    <Cropper.Area aria-label="Crop area" />
  </Cropper.Viewport>
</Cropper.Root>
\`\`\`

## use an item outside a group

outside \`AspectGroup\`, an item is a plain button with \`aria-pressed\` instead of a radio:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.AspectItem value={1}>square</Cropper.AspectItem>
\`\`\`

## turn the orientation icon

\`Orientation\` says which way the crop faces in \`data-orientation\`. this turns its icon for portrait:

\`\`\`css
[data-zriz-item="orientation"] {
  &[data-orientation="portrait"] svg {
    rotate: 90deg;
  }
}
\`\`\`

a press swaps the ratio for its inverse, so 4:5 becomes 5:4. it springs like an item pick, and \`onValueChange\` gets the reason \`orientation\`.

## follow the orientation in the labels

after a swap the crop is 5:4, so a 4:5 item is no longer checked. to keep one item per ratio, flip the values and labels with the orientation. render it inside \`Root\`:

\`\`\`tsx
"use client";

import { useCropperState } from "@zriz/react";
import * as Cropper from "@zriz/react/cropper";

const RATIOS = [
  [4, 5],
  [3, 4],
  [9, 16],
] as const;

export const Ratios = () => {
  const aspect = useCropperState((s) => s.aspect);
  const wide = typeof aspect === "number" && aspect > 1;
  return (
    <Cropper.AspectGroup aria-label="Aspect ratio">
      <Cropper.AspectItem value="free">free</Cropper.AspectItem>
      <Cropper.AspectItem value={1}>1:1</Cropper.AspectItem>
      {RATIOS.map(([w, h]) => (
        <Cropper.AspectItem
          key={\`\${w}:\${h}\`}
          value={wide ? h / w : w / h}
        >
          {wide ? \`\${h}:\${w}\` : \`\${w}:\${h}\`}
        </Cropper.AspectItem>
      ))}
    </Cropper.AspectGroup>
  );
};
\`\`\`

## keyboard

the group is one tab stop. tab lands on the checked item, or on the first one when none is checked. the arrows move and select at once:

| key | what it does |
| - | - |
| \`right\` or \`down\` | select the next ratio |
| \`left\` or \`up\` | select the previous ratio |
| \`home\` or \`end\` | select the first or the last ratio |

the arrows wrap around at the ends and skip disabled items. with \`dir="rtl"\` on \`Root\`, left and right swap.

## api

### \`AspectGroup\`

renders a \`<div role="radiogroup">\` anywhere inside \`Root\`. every part also takes \`className\`, \`render\` and the props of its element, see [composition](https://zriz.dev/docs/composition.md). \`className\` and \`render\` get \`{ aspect }\`.

- \`aria-label\` \`string\`

  names the group for screen readers

### \`AspectItem\`

renders a \`<button type="button">\`, with \`role="radio"\` inside \`AspectGroup\`. \`className\` and \`render\` get \`{ checked, disabled }\`.

- \`value\` \`"free" | "original" | number\` required

  the ratio this item picks, as width / height

| attribute | when |
| - | - |
| \`data-checked\` | while this ratio is the current one |
| \`data-disabled\` | on a round crop, for every value but 1 |

### \`Orientation\`

renders a \`<button type="button">\` anywhere inside \`Root\`. it has no props of its own. it is \`disabled\` while the aspect is 1, \`"free"\` or \`"original"\`. \`className\` and \`render\` get \`{ orientation }\`.

| attribute | when |
| - | - |
| \`data-orientation\` | \`"landscape"\` above 1, \`"portrait"\` below 1, \`"square"\` at 1 and while the aspect is \`"free"\` or \`"original"\` |
"
`;

exports[`content > writes avatar as markdown 1`] = `
"# avatar

> [llms.txt](https://zriz.dev/llms.txt)

a profile photo picker: the visitor picks a file, moves it under a circle and saves a round png.

the demo runs on the page at https\\://zriz.dev/docs/avatar.

## take a file from the visitor

\`src\` takes the \`File\` from the input as it is. picking a new file turns save off until that photo loads.

each pick bumps a counter that \`Root\` takes as its \`key\`, so every photo starts from the full frame. [loading images](https://zriz.dev/docs/loading-images.md) explains why.

\`\`\`tsx
<input
  type="file"
  accept="image/*"
  onChange={(event) => {
    setStatus("empty");
    setSaveFailed(false);
    setPicks((count) => count + 1);
    setFile(event.target.files?.[0] ?? null);
  }}
/>
\`\`\`

## crop to a circle

\`shape="circle"\` locks the aspect to 1 and draws a round mask. the area has no handles, so the visitor drags the photo under the circle and zooms it with a pinch or, with \`wheel="zoom"\`, the mouse wheel.

\`minSize\` keeps the crop at least 512 by 512 source pixels. on a photo with a side under 512 px, the circle stays as large as the photo allows. \`onLoad\` fires when the photo has decoded and turns save on.

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Root
  key={picks}
  actionsRef={actions}
  src={file}
  shape="circle"
  minSize={{ width: 512, height: 512 }}
  onLoad={() => setStatus("ready")}
  onError={() => setStatus("failed")}
>
  <Cropper.Viewport
    wheel="zoom"
    style={{ width: 320, height: 320 }}
  >
    <Cropper.Image />
    <Cropper.Mask />
    <Cropper.Area aria-label="Crop area" />
  </Cropper.Viewport>
</Cropper.Root>
\`\`\`

## say when a photo does not open

\`onError\` gets a \`ZrizError\` when the file is not a photo or the browser cannot decode it, such as a heic file in chrome. the alert asks for another file. [errors](https://zriz.dev/docs/errors.md) lists every code.

\`\`\`tsx
const unreadable =
  "this photo does not open. pick a jpeg, png or webp.";

{status === "failed" && <p role="alert">{unreadable}</p>}
\`\`\`

## save a png

\`exportCrop\` reads the circle from \`Root\` and returns a png with transparent corners, at most 512 by 512. it comes from \`@zriz/core/dom\`. add \`@zriz/core\` as in [exporting](https://zriz.dev/docs/exporting.md).

an export can still fail on a very large photo, so \`save\` shows its own alert when it does.

\`\`\`tsx
const unsaved = "this crop did not save. try again.";

const save = async () => {
  if (!actions.current) return;
  try {
    const { blob } = await exportCrop(actions.current, {
      maxSize: { width: 512, height: 512 },
    });
    setSaveFailed(false);
    onSave(blob);
  } catch {
    setSaveFailed(true);
  }
};

{saveFailed && <p role="alert">{unsaved}</p>}

<button
  type="button"
  disabled={status !== "ready"}
  onClick={save}
>
  save
</button>
\`\`\`

## the whole file

\`AvatarPicker\` hands \`onSave\` the png as a \`Blob\`:

\`\`\`tsx
"use client";

import { exportCrop } from "@zriz/core/dom";
import type { Cropper as CropperApi } from "@zriz/react";
import * as Cropper from "@zriz/react/cropper";
import "@zriz/react/styles.css";
import { useRef, useState } from "react";

type Props = { onSave: (png: Blob) => void };
type Status = "empty" | "ready" | "failed";

const unreadable =
  "this photo does not open. pick a jpeg, png or webp.";
const unsaved = "this crop did not save. try again.";

export const AvatarPicker = ({ onSave }: Props) => {
  const [file, setFile] = useState<File | null>(null);
  const [status, setStatus] = useState<Status>("empty");
  const [saveFailed, setSaveFailed] = useState(false);
  const [picks, setPicks] = useState(0);
  const actions = useRef<CropperApi>(null);

  const save = async () => {
    if (!actions.current) return;
    try {
      const { blob } = await exportCrop(actions.current, {
        maxSize: { width: 512, height: 512 },
      });
      setSaveFailed(false);
      onSave(blob);
    } catch {
      setSaveFailed(true);
    }
  };

  return (
    <>
      <input
        type="file"
        accept="image/*"
        onChange={(event) => {
          setStatus("empty");
          setSaveFailed(false);
          setPicks((count) => count + 1);
          setFile(event.target.files?.[0] ?? null);
        }}
      />
      <Cropper.Root
        key={picks}
        actionsRef={actions}
        src={file}
        shape="circle"
        minSize={{ width: 512, height: 512 }}
        onLoad={() => setStatus("ready")}
        onError={() => setStatus("failed")}
      >
        <Cropper.Viewport
          wheel="zoom"
          style={{ width: 320, height: 320 }}
        >
          <Cropper.Image />
          <Cropper.Mask />
          <Cropper.Area aria-label="Crop area" />
        </Cropper.Viewport>
      </Cropper.Root>
      {status === "failed" && <p role="alert">{unreadable}</p>}
      {saveFailed && <p role="alert">{unsaved}</p>}
      <button
        type="button"
        disabled={status !== "ready"}
        onClick={save}
      >
        save
      </button>
    </>
  );
};
\`\`\`
"
`;

exports[`content > writes bundle-size as markdown 1`] = `
"# bundle size

> [llms.txt](https://zriz.dev/llms.txt)

what each set of imports adds to your bundle, minified and compressed with brotli.

## first load

| set | imports | brotli |
| - | - | - |
| editor | every part from \`@zriz/react/cropper\` | 22.14 kB |
| avatar | \`Root\`, \`Viewport\`, \`Image\`, \`Mask\`, \`Area\` | 17.00 kB |
| root only | \`Root\` | 11.79 kB |
| vanilla avatar | \`createCropper\`, \`loadImage\`, \`attachImage\`, \`bindViewport\`, \`bindPhoto\`, \`bindMask\` and \`bindArea\` | 14.64 kB |
| server | \`toSharp\` from \`@zriz/core\` | 540 B |
| stylesheet | \`styles.css\`, which is optional | 842 B |

measured with size-limit 14.3 on 4 november 2026. it bundles each set with rolldown, minifies it and compresses it with brotli, and it leaves out react and react-dom. the build uses the \`production\` export condition, so development warnings do not count.

with gzip, the stylesheet is 968 B.

## loaded later

four chunks stay out of the first load and download the first time a photo needs them. each row is what the chunk adds to the avatar set:

| chunk | loads when | brotli |
| - | - | - |
| render | the first export. it starts downloading once the first photo attaches | 1.92 kB |
| sharpen | the sharper redraw at rest and on deep zoom. it starts downloading after the first paint | 393 B |
| svg | the photo is an svg | 564 B |
| source | you pass an \`img\`, \`video\`, \`canvas\` or \`OffscreenCanvas\` to \`loadImage\`. \`Root\` never loads it | 325 B |

with all four chunks, even \`source\`, which \`Root\` never loads, the avatar set comes to 20.20 kB. your bundler keeps the code a chunk shares with the first load in the first load, so the chunks stay this small. a chunk bundled alone is larger: \`render\` is 2.89 kB.

## dependencies

\`@zriz/react\` depends only on \`@zriz/core\`, which has no dependencies. both packages mark only their css as a side effect, so your bundler drops every part you do not import.
"
`;

exports[`content > writes buttons as markdown 1`] = `
"# buttons

> [llms.txt](https://zriz.dev/llms.txt)

\`Rotate\` turns the photo a quarter turn, \`Flip\` mirrors it and \`Reset\` undoes every change.

the demo runs on the page at https\\://zriz.dev/docs/buttons.

## anatomy

each one is a button that goes anywhere inside \`Root\`. put an icon or a word inside, and give an icon-only button an \`aria-label\`:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Rotate aria-label="Rotate left">
  <svg
    aria-hidden="true"
    width={20}
    height={20}
    viewBox="0 0 20 20"
  >
    <path
      d="M4 4v4h4M4.5 8a6 6 0 1 1 1.5 6.5"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      strokeWidth={1.5}
    />
  </svg>
</Cropper.Rotate>
<Cropper.Flip aria-label="Flip">
  <svg
    aria-hidden="true"
    width={20}
    height={20}
    viewBox="0 0 20 20"
  >
    <path
      d="M10 3v14M7 5l-4 10h4zM13 5l4 10h-4z"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      strokeWidth={1.5}
    />
  </svg>
</Cropper.Flip>
<Cropper.Reset>reset</Cropper.Reset>
\`\`\`

zriz ships them bare, with no paint and no icons. the demo above uses the icons and styles from the zriz site.

## see what each button moves

| part | what it does |
| - | - |
| \`Rotate\` | turns the photo 90°, easing out. a 3:2 crop becomes 2:3 |
| \`Flip\` | mirrors the photo, left to right by default, with a spring |
| \`Reset\` | springs back to where the crop started: \`defaultValue\` and the starting \`aspect\` and \`rotation\`, or the full photo |

while \`Root\` is disabled, a press does nothing, and before the photo loads only \`Reset\` acts. the buttons stay enabled, so style them from \`data-disabled\` on \`Root\`, as [root](https://zriz.dev/docs/root.md) shows.

while a move runs, \`Root\` carries \`data-transition\`: \`"rotate"\`, \`"flip"\` or \`"morph"\` for \`Reset\`. [accessibility](https://zriz.dev/docs/accessibility.md) lists how long each move takes, with and without reduced motion.

## rotate both ways

\`Rotate\` turns left, like ios photos. \`direction="cw"\` turns right:

\`\`\`tsx
<Cropper.Rotate>rotate left</Cropper.Rotate>
<Cropper.Rotate direction="cw">rotate right</Cropper.Rotate>
\`\`\`

## keep reset hidden

\`Reset\` hides with the \`hidden\` attribute while nothing has changed. if a class sets \`display\` on it, add this rule:

\`\`\`css
[data-zriz-item="reset"][hidden] {
  display: none;
}
\`\`\`

## api

### \`Rotate\`

renders a \`<button type="button">\` anywhere inside \`Root\`. every part also takes \`className\`, \`render\` and the props of its element, see [composition](https://zriz.dev/docs/composition.md).

- \`direction\` \`"ccw" | "cw"\` = \`"ccw"\`

  \`"ccw"\` turns left, \`"cw"\` turns right

### \`Flip\`

renders a \`<button type="button">\` with \`aria-pressed\` anywhere inside \`Root\`. \`className\` and \`render\` get \`{ mirrored }\`.

- \`axis\` \`"x" | "y"\` = \`"x"\`

  \`"x"\` swaps left and right, \`"y"\` swaps top and bottom

| attribute | when |
| - | - |
| \`data-mirrored\` | while the photo is mirrored, with \`aria-pressed="true"\` |

### \`Reset\`

renders a \`<button type="button">\` anywhere inside \`Root\`. it has no props of its own. \`className\` and \`render\` get \`{ pristine }\`.

| attribute | when |
| - | - |
| \`data-pristine\` | while nothing has changed. the button is \`hidden\` then |
"
`;

exports[`content > writes changelog as markdown 1`] = `
"# changelog

> [llms.txt](https://zriz.dev/llms.txt)

what changed in each published version of zriz, newest first.

## 0.0.0, not published yet

the first version. nothing is on npm yet, so there is nothing to upgrade from. [introduction](https://zriz.dev/docs/introduction.md) lists what it does.
"
